# The fault reasons each board in this folder raises on purpose.
#
# Format: one line per board that faults, with fields separated by a single space:
#
#   <board path> <reason> [<reason> ...]
#
# Each reason is a FaultReason name, listed once, in byte order. Lines are sorted byte-wise by
# board path. A board with no line raises no fault.
#
# crates/fabrico-engine/tests/board_faults.rs plays every board, reads the reason of each fault it
# raises, and fails when they differ from the board's line here. The docs site's build fails when a
# page's <Board faultsAbout="..."> names other reasons than the board's line. Edit this file by
# hand: when a board's faults change, the test's failure message gives the line to write.
examples/boards/demo_scene.board.ron FactoryError
examples/boards/docs/faults-branch-busy.board.ron BranchBusy
examples/boards/docs/faults-command-failure.board.ron CommandFailure
examples/boards/docs/faults-command-timeout.board.ron CommandTimeout
examples/boards/docs/faults-factory-error.board.ron FactoryError
examples/boards/docs/faults-factory-timeout.board.ron FactoryTimeout
examples/boards/docs/faults-no-entry-wire.board.ron NoEntryWire
examples/boards/docs/faults-no-match.board.ron NoMatch
examples/boards/docs/faults-wire-overflow.board.ron WireOverflow
examples/boards/docs/rules-machine-states.board.ron NoMatch
examples/boards/docs/script-outcomes.board.ron CommandFailure CommandTimeout
